# The density every app starts at: the user's main monitor's, which the host puts on the kernel
# command line each boot (androidboot.lcd_density, and androidboot.dsa.display_dpi for the
# hwcomposer; 130 at a scale of 100%, 196 at 150%). SurfaceFlinger reads it from
# ro.sf.lcd_density, so no build.prop sets that property: a build.prop value is read before this
# script and would keep every boot at the image's density. Cuttlefish's vendor script sets the
# same property from the same boot argument; whichever runs first sets it, to the same value.
# An app that started at another density than its window's monitor would be relaunched as soon
# as the window asked for the right one.
on early-init
    setprop ro.sf.lcd_density ${ro.boot.lcd_density:-130}
